; The structured SSA computation IR: typed values, regions, the builder, the
; verifier, the printer and the reference interpreter. Pure OCaml: no native
; process API, no physical target, no tensor or graph type. Beyond [core],
; [err_trace], [expr] and [fmt] it sees only the descriptor libraries
; (attention, contraction, norm blocks and [f32_math]), none of which owns a
; tensor or graph type, so source lowering and the Loop comparison bridge
; depend on it and never the reverse. See the SSA design in .ai/.
;
; Wrapped (default): consumers write [Ssa_ir.Ssa_builder].

(library
 (name ssa_ir)
 (libraries
  attention_block
  attention_layer_block
  contraction
  core
  err_trace
  expr
  f32_math
  fmt
  norm_block))
